From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:56:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] spu: late-combine off unless requested (it drops
 DImode-to-SImode truncations)

Found by the stage 4 A/B: libsheap cellSheapQueryFree returned the high word of
its 64-bit count (0) because late-combine removed the shlqbyi of the
truncation; -fno-late-combine-instructions restores it.
---
 gcc/config/spu/spu.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc b/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
index f84a39d9d6e..8f62c95ff73 100644
--- a/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
@@ -252,6 +252,14 @@ spu_option_override (void)
   if (!OPTION_SET_P (flag_tree_loop_distribute_patterns) && optimize < 3)
     flag_tree_loop_distribute_patterns = 0;
 
+  /* late-combine (GCC 15) substitutes a DImode-to-SImode lowpart as if the
+     truncation were free; on SPU it is not (TRULY_NOOP_TRUNCATION: a SImode
+     value lives in word 0 of the register, the low word of a DImode value in
+     word 1), so  lost its shift and returned the high word
+     (libsheap cellSheapQueryFree).  Off unless requested, as before GCC 15.  */
+  if (!OPTION_SET_P (flag_late_combine_instructions))
+    flag_late_combine_instructions = 0;
+
   /* Functions must be 8 byte aligned so we correctly handle dual issue */
   parse_alignment_opts ();
   if (align_functions.levels[0].get_value () < 8)
